WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.000
- So this past September,
a dream was realized

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.650
when the Academy Museum of
Motion Pictures opened its doors.

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:09.870
A museum like this comes
with a hefty price tag,

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.320
482 million dollars.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.140
And I know many people in
this room donated generously.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:19.213
I did my part, and this weekend,

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.260
this past weekend, I paid a visit

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.585
to see where my $15 went.

00:00:24.585 --> 00:00:26.906
(audience laughing)

00:00:26.906 --> 00:00:29.656
(dramatic music)

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.110
Barbara Streisand Bridge.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:35.100
Wonder how much she donated to get this.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.080
I knew I should've went up to 25 bucks.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:39.750
- Excuse me, can I help you?

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.100
- Yeah, I'm here to see my stuff.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.000
- Oh, the ticket booth is right over here.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.380
- I'm Wanda Sykes.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.780
I'm a donor.
- What level?

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:50.000
- 15 big ones.
- 15,000?

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.100
Oh, Ms. Sykes.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.490
- That's tax deductible, right?

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:56.600
I know some of these people.
- That's our donor wall.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:57.920
Okay, come on in.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:00.170
- Ah, go ahead, I'll,
I'll catch up with you.

00:01:02.828 --> 00:01:04.500
(audience laughing)

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.980
- [Tom] This is one of
our most popular exhibits.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.010
- Oh, you ain't gotta
tell me what this is.

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:11.370
Billy Porter, Kinky Boots.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:14.623
Originally, it was called
Kinky Kitten Heels.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:18.570
- They're the ruby slippers.

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:21.550
- Tom, you got this whole
room for the "Wizard of Oz,"

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:23.800
and this is the only thing
you got from "The Wiz?"

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:25.506
Wait, I got this.

00:01:25.506 --> 00:01:26.900
(audience laughing)

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.440
You ever been to Meryl Streep's house?

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.195
- Mm-mm.
- Looks just like this.

00:01:30.195 --> 00:01:31.028
(audience laughing)

00:01:31.028 --> 00:01:33.280
- This is a very important display.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:36.650
Hattie McDaniel was the
first Black Oscar winner.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:40.580
Her award went missing after
she donated it to a university.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:41.413
- DeVry?

00:01:41.413 --> 00:01:42.246
(audience laughing)

00:01:42.246 --> 00:01:44.563
- And this empty case
honors her historic win.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:50.093
- It also honors all the
Oscars won by Black directors.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.560
- I'm sure you will recognize
this famous Oscar gown

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:55.700
worn by-
- Little Richard.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:56.870
- Cher.
- Cher.

00:01:56.870 --> 00:02:00.910
- In 1986, when she
presented at the Oscars,

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:03.220
but didn't receive a nomination.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.160
- Ah see, this is what you wear

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.680
when you break up with Oscar.

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:08.740
This is like the ultimate revenge gown.

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:10.827
'Cause it says, "You could've had this.

00:02:10.827 --> 00:02:12.794
"You could've had all this."

00:02:12.794 --> 00:02:13.627
(audience laughing)

00:02:13.627 --> 00:02:17.440
- Everything in this room
belongs to Mr. Spike Lee.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.450
- Wait a minute, he just left it here?

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.170
How much y'all charging him for storage?

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:24.110
- The Academy isn't
charging Mr. Lee anything.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.140
- Wait a minute, he
stores it here for free?

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:27.400
Okay, I gotta get in on this,

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.472
'cause I'm paying 250 out in Glendale.

00:02:29.472 --> 00:02:31.030
(audience laughing)

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.817
Is it 24-hour access?

00:02:32.817 --> 00:02:35.500
(intriguing music)

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.630
- Ooh, white chicks.

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:40.193
That Marlon Wayans was hilarious.

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:43.280
- This is from-
- "Aquaman," Jason Momoa.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:46.640
- No, this is Guillermo
del Toro's creature

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.930
from "The Shape of Water."

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.800
- Well, you didn't see Jason Momoa

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:53.614
after filming all day underwater.

00:02:53.614 --> 00:02:56.950
(audience chuckling)

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:58.390
Hey, Harvey Weinstein.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:01.550
(audience laughing)

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:04.510
- Here we have film
history with over 700 films

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:06.700
from the Lumiere brothers to present day.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.290
- You know, they have monitors
like this at Best Buy.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:10.470
You pick the one you want,

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:12.320
and they load it right into your car.

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:14.630
I'm gonna take this one.

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:15.693
Come grab an end.

00:03:15.693 --> 00:03:16.526
(audience laughing)

00:03:16.526 --> 00:03:18.643
- No, no, no, Ms. Sykes.

